 "asked_at": "2026-10-18T00:45+08:00",
 "answer": "Yes, the haze is bad in KL today. Air quality is in the \"unhealthy\" range.\n\n- As of 9.30am on Saturday, Oct 17, Cheras in Kuala Lumpur recorded an API of 162 and Batu Muda 159, while Putrajaya also registered 162.\n- 24 areas nationwide were in the unhealthy range, and Pasir Gudang, Johor, was the highest at 196.\n- Nearby areas were also affected. In Selangor, Klang recorded 171, and Petaling Jaya and Shah Alam 169 each.\n\nThe API scale works like this: 0 to 50 is good, 51 to 100 moderate, 101 to 200 unhealthy, 201 to 300 very unhealthy, and above 300 hazardous. KL's readings are in the upper half of \"unhealthy\" but below \"very unhealthy\".\n\nThe haze has lasted several days. Reports from earlier this week showed similar or worse levels, such as Johan Setia at 184 and Klang at 176 on Oct 16. Don't expect a quick improvement.\n\n**Precautions:**\n- Limit strenuous outdoor activity, especially if you're a child, elderly, pregnant, or have asthma or heart or lung conditions.\n- Wear a well-fitted N95 or KN95 mask if you go out.\n- Keep windows closed, and use an air purifier or air-con on recirculate if you have one.\n\nReadings change through the day. For the latest numbers, check the Department of Environment's MyAQI/APIMS or the DOE's official channels.",
